Missing records after compacting

This is fixing an issue.
The Transactions were being looked up without the readLock and some of the controls for Read and Write lock
were broken.

Here is the root cause:
The `getSyncCallback()` method in `JournalBase.java` conditionally returned `null` when `supportsCallback` was `false`, even when `sync` was `true`. Because of this, `JournalImpl`'s `appendAddRecord`/`appendUpdateRecord` methods (which used `if (result != null) result.get()` guards) could skip waiting on the `SimpleFuture` result of the asynchronous append executor task. This broke the synchronization contract between the calling thread and the append executor, meaning the write lock/read lock coordination around journal appends and transaction bookkeeping (`pendingTransactions`, `newTransactions`) was not properly enforced. As a result, the `JournalCompactor` could read and process transactions/records concurrently while appends were still in-flight and not yet protected by the proper read lock, causing pending transactions and their associated records to be missed or inconsistently compacted (missing records after compacting).

